{"id": "tea:tattvatraya:1", "source": "src:tattvatraya", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Cit: the soul is distinct from body, senses, mind, breath and intellect; it is self-luminous, blissful, eternal, atomic, imperceptible, unthinkable, partless, unchanging, the substrate of knowledge, controlled, supported and owned by the Lord; souls are bound, freed or eternal.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:jiva", "cpt:classes-of-souls", "cpt:tattvatraya"], "teachers": ["tch:pillai-lokacarya"], "speaker": "Piḷḷai Lokācārya", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tattvatraya:2", "source": "src:tattvatraya", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "Acit: insentient reality is of three kinds — pure sattva (the substance of Vaikuṇṭha and the Lord's forms), mixed sattva (prakṛti with the three guṇas, the stuff of bodies and worlds) and that devoid of sattva (time).", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "terms": ["trm:suddha-sattva", "trm:misra-sattva", "trm:sattva-sunya"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-kinds-of-acit", "cpt:tattvatraya"], "teachers": ["tch:pillai-lokacarya"], "speaker": "Piḷḷai Lokācārya", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tattvatraya:3", "source": "src:tattvatraya", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "Īśvara: the Lord is opposed to all evil and has infinite auspicious qualities; he is the cause of the world, its self and support, present in five forms — the supreme, the vyūhas, the descents, the inner controller and the image.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:ubhaya-linga", "cpt:five-forms-of-god-pancaratra", "cpt:tattvatraya"], "teachers": ["tch:pillai-lokacarya"], "speaker": "Piḷḷai Lokācārya", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
